Consumer platform plus runner plus isolation plus cache plus ordering stay
qualified with fixture evidence (issue #509).

Four explicit platform identifiers with no implicit default: linux_x86_64,
linux_arm64 native (issue #410), macos_arm64 native (issue #412),
windows_x86_64 native MSVC-compatible (issue #414). macOS x86_64 is Not
planned per issue #976 with no runner. Missing, empty, or unsupported
selections fail closed in platforms-gate before any per-platform job queues
a runner (must be a nonempty JSON array, unsupported platforms rejected,
no implicit default, not skipped validation or platform substitution).

Runner routing never falls through: linux_x86_64 to ubuntu-latest,
linux_arm64 to ubuntu-24.04-arm, macos_arm64 to macos-14,
windows_x86_64 to windows-latest with shell bash.
Linux arm64 never reaches the macOS runner; Windows never reaches macOS.

Isolation is per-job checkouts with persist-credentials false on separate
runners: nine actions/checkout uses with persist-credentials false,
per-platform test/build/coverage wait on needs platforms-gate while
Linux-once lint/typecheck/format/generate/security-audit/license-audit
never do, timeout-minutes per job with fail-fast false matrices. No
shared Bazel output-base lock is advertised: do not advertise parallelism
while jobs serialize on one shared Bazel output-base lock. Each job
passes --noshow_progress to Bazel invocations.

Cache is absent in the reusable workflow (no actions/cache in
reusable-consumer): consumers get cold caches per job. Per-host disk-cache
scopes live in ci.yml only (bazel-seed-, bazel-arm64-, bazel-musl-x86_64-,
bazel-musl-arm64-, bazel-macos-arm64-,
bazel-windows-x86_64-), free-tier eligible with no paid services.

Ordering is parallel only: scheduling_mode parallel is the default and
the template schedules parallel only until sequential ordering is
qualified. scheduling_mode sequential is qualification-open and fails
closed; any other non-parallel value is rejected as unsupported
scheduling_mode. In both modes failures preserve completed results, fail
the overall run, and do not cancel independent checks.

Seed only for platform plus consumer plus release evidence; no
Supported claim. Live multi-host consumer execution beyond the seed
stays owned under issues #298/#410/#411/#412/#414.
